  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "The Smart Traveler Enrollment Program (STEP) is a free U.S. Department of State service for citizens traveling/living abroad to receive emergency alerts and assistance. It works by allowing users to register trip details online to receive security updates. Eligibility includes all U.S. citizens and nationals, and enrollment is done via the STEP website. Key Aspects of STEP (Travel): How it Works: Sends email alerts regarding safety, natural disasters, or, and helps embassies contact you during emergencies. Eligibility: Open to U.S. citizens and nationals traveling or residing abroad (tourists, students, residents). Enrollment: Takes about 20 minutes to complete on the official website. Other \"Step\" Terms: Step App (Money): A banking application (step.com) designed to build credit, offering savings, cashback, and no-fee accounts for teens/young adults. State Trade Expansion Program (STEP): An SBA-funded program that provides grants to help small businesses export their products. STEP (Travel) Enrollment:You can enroll online at the Smart Traveler Enrollment Program website. Step All-in-One Money App:This is a financial tool allowing users to build credit for free, receive up to 10% cash back, and access savings, as described by step.com. It is geared toward building credit without an existing credit score.",
